rst law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T17:37:33-07:00","id":1479625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479609-scion-type-examples?p=1479620#post1479620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For wonder woman I am pretty sure she is nowadays a daughter of zeus, and iirc in the animated universe her father is ares. Regardless, the other two will be added, thank you for the input.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, in the Justice League/Justice League Unlimited series i'm pretty sure the implication was of her being a daughter of Hypolita with <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7iPjnE2T6GM\" target=\"_blank\">Hades</a> (though the <a href=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/DBVj-QCU0AAVYG1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">visual inspiration</a> can't be denied)....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-27-2022, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T17:38:26-07:00","id":1479626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479609-scion-type-examples?p=1479625#post1479625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, in the Justice League/Justice League Unlimited series i'm pretty sure the implication was of her being a daughter of Hypolita with Hades....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahh that does sound familiar, my bad, thank you for the correction. I do not have HBO max so I've not seen Justice League Unlimited for a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T19:11:45-07:00","id":1479634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479609-scion-type-examples?p=1479619#post1479619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder Woman in her post-Crisis origin as a Created. <br /> <br /> Galatea from the story of Pygmalion (most commonly from Ovid's Metamorphosis) as a Created of Venus/Aphrodite. <br /> <br /> Odysseus as a Chosen of Athena (arguably).</div> </div> </div> </div>Odysseus was a potential Scion (Origin level character with a Calling) by virtue of his blood descent from Hermes by way of Autolycus, but his Visitation was Athena, so he\u2019s be Chosen in that his patron is not his parent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T20:00:56-07:00","id":1479637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479609-scion-type-examples?p=1479626#post1479626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ahh that does sound familiar, my bad, thank you for the correction. I do not have HBO max so I've not seen Justice League Unlimited for a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's alright and completely understandable. Damn, i remember that arc so many years later <b>because </b>of the implications and how much Hades was obviously an expy of Perez's Ares.<br /> <br /> As an aside, Ares did make at least one appearance in the JLU, though with a different <a href=\"https://br.pinterest.com/pin/465348573969205786/\" target=\"_blank\">look</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-27-2022, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T02:31:59-07:00","id":1479651,"title":"","content":"The Celts loved their incarnations. Unfortunately, I am at best an interested amateur when it comes to Celtic mythology, but I don't think Watcher comes around here any more, so I'll do my best to list off what I'm mostly certain about.<br /> <br /> Cu Chulainn is almost certainly an incarnation of Lugh, though in later versions he fits more in the born category (mostly later versions, likely a reaction to Christianization).<br /> <br /> Cu Roi might also be an incarnation/born of Lugh... if so, he was killed by his self/brother/son/father Cu Chulainn, no doubt leading to many uncomfortable family reunions.<br /> <br /> Pryderi is likely the incarnation of the Welsh maybe-diety, Mabon ap Modron, which is likely an aspect or offshoot of the more widespread Celtic deity Maponos.<br /> <br /> There's a decent case that Gawain, nephew of King Arthur, is a partially-Christianized amalgamation of all of the above (mostly but not exclusively Cu Chulainn), so you could call him an incarnation of Lugh. At some point, Percival was also associated with Pryderi, though I think the scholarly consensus may have swung away from that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T14:02:36-07:00","id":1479668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479609-scion-type-examples?p=1479651#post1479651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Celts loved their incarnations. Unfortunately, I am at best an interested amateur when it comes to Celtic mythology, but I don't think Watcher comes around here any more, so I'll do my best to list off what I'm mostly certain about.<br /> <br /> Cu Chulainn is almost certainly an incarnation of Lugh, though in later versions he fits more in the born category (mostly later versions, likely a reaction to Christianization).<br /> <br /> Cu Roi might also be an incarnation/born of Lugh... if so, he was killed by his self/brother/son/father Cu Chulainn, no doubt leading to many uncomfortable family reunions.<br /> <br /> Pryderi is likely the incarnation of the Welsh maybe-diety, Mabon ap Modron, which is likely an aspect or offshoot of the more widespread Celtic deity Maponos.<br /> <br /> There's a decent case that Gawain, nephew of King Arthur, is a partially-Christianized amalgamation of all of the above (mostly but not exclusively Cu Chulainn), so you could call him an incarnation of Lugh. At some point, Percival was also associated with Pryderi, though I think the scholarly consensus may have swung away from that one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh boy that's a lot. Adding now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T20:26:39-07:00","id":1479675,"title":"","content":"I think I remember <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> saying that \u201cCuChulain = Lugh\u201d came from a transcription error, but I donMt remember for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T13:58:53-07:00","id":1479741,"title":"","content":"Appreciated, but if you do not mind I would rather wait till that is confirmed to do any changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T10:29:35-07:00","id":1479960,"title":"","content":"Tia Dalma from the Pirates of the Caribbean series works as an incarnate version of the goddess Calypso.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T12:15:19-07:00","id":1479968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479609-scion-type-examples?p=1479960#post1479960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tia Dalma from the Pirates of the Caribbean series works as an incarnate version of the goddess Calypso.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you, I forgot about her.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T21:21:45-07:00","id":1480014,"title":"","content":"So what would one make, like, Lucoa from Dragon Maid? Cuz normally I would say an incarnate of Quetzalcoatl, but they make it quite clear she's a dragon. Then again, it's a likely theory that Quetzalcoatl is a Serpent flight dragon that joined the Teotl anyway. So, both? Neither?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T22:18:03-07:00","id":1480341,"title":"","content":"For some more Anime/JRPG examples (well, really just examples in general, but oh well), here's a few:<br /> <br /> Born: Erice Utsemi (Izanami; Fate), Sailor Pluto (Chronos; Sailor Moon), the Bhaalspawn (Bhaal; Baldur's Gate)<br /> Chosen: Nanashi the Godslayer (Dagda; Shin Megami Tensei IV), The Demifiend (Lucifer; SMT Nocturne)<br /> Created: Enkidu (Aruru; Epic of Gilgamesh), Rei Ayanami (Lilith; Neon Genesis Evangelion)<br /> Incarnated: Tamamo-no-Mae (Amaterasu; Fate), Seto Kaiba (Set; YuGiOh), Byleth (Sothis; Fire Emblem 3 Houses), Zelda (Hylia; Legend of Zelda Skyward Sword)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T18:23:58-07:00","id":1480434,"title":"","content":"Seto Kaiba is a reincarnation of Set!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T19:35:04-07:00","id":1481272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479609-scion-type-examples?p=1480434#post1480434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seto Kaiba is a reincarnation of Set!?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's the reincarnation of the Egyptian *priest* Set, who later gets deified as the &quot;God&quot; Set. Same with all of the other Egyptian deities that aren't the Egyptian God Cards (Ra, Osiris and Obelisk basically.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T18:13:45-07:00","id":1481883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479609-scion-type-examples?p=1481272#post1481272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's the reincarnation of the Egyptian *priest* Set, who later gets deified as the &quot;God&quot; Set. Same with all of the other Egyptian deities that aren't the Egyptian God Cards (Ra, Osiris and Obelisk basically.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Obelisk is not a god, it's a type of monument. Though what does that make Yami?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T23:15:44-07:00","id":1481900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479609-scion-type-examples?p=1481883#post1481883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Obelisk is not a god, it's a type of monument. Though what does that make Yami?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Yugioh Obelisk the Tormentor is the name of one of the 3 Egyptian God Cards, his name is presumably turned into a word through generations of lost history until it becomes the name of a stone pillar in our time. As for Yami/Atem, even though his name is technically &quot;lost to the ages,&quot; he still shares a name with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atum\" target=\"_blank\">Atum.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}